    99	# install jupyterlab
   100	pip install jupyterlab
   101	# launch jupyterlab
   102	jupyter-lab
   103	```
   104	
   105	2. Following that, download our dataset release from: https://github.com/sola-st/github-workflow-resource-optimization/releases/tag/v1.0.0
   106	3. Unzip the dataset in the same folder as this README file.
   107	
   108	## Running the Artifact
   109	
   110	### Data Collection
   111	In this part, we present the necessary resources and instructions to replicate our data collection process (or collect more data).
   112	
   113	#### Collection resources
   114	* [repositories.csv](./repositories.csv): This is the list of popular repositories ([reference to this work](https://decan.lexpage.net/files/ICSME-2022.pdf)) from which we randomly sampled 600 repositories to use them in our study.
   115	
   116	* [repositories-2021-03-08.zip](./repositories-2021-03-08.csv): The list containing unpopular repositories ([reference to this work](https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.04682)) from which we randomly sampled 74K candidates to collect workflows data. We ended up with 352 repositories having such data.
   117	
   118	* [Collection notebook](./collect.ipynb): This is the code (in notebook format) used to collect our data using the two repositories lists as input.
   119	
   120	
   121	#### How to run?
   122	To run the collection code:
   123	1. Open the notebook [Collection notebook](./collect.ipynb).
   124	2. Open the file [tokens.json](./tokens.json) and add your GitHub tokens into the file. To have a non-interrupted collection, we used 4 tokens at a time granting 20K requests per hour in total.
   125	Here is an example of how the tokens.json file should look like:
   126	    ```json
   127	    [
   128	        "here you put token 1",
   129	        "here you put token 2",
   130	    ]
   131	    ```
   132	3. Run the cells of the notebook one after another.
   133	
   134	#### Resulting Data
   135	Applying the above collection process we obtained the following data files (In case you are viewing this on GitHub, the links below wouldn't work but you can find all the files within [this relase](https://github.com/sola-st/github-workflow-resource-optimization/releases/tag/v1.0.0)):
